      "content": "I see what you mean about the coastal vibe. But I actually read something else online that suggested this specific phrase is a traditional way to acknowledge the resilience of the people in that specific province, even if they are near the coast. It's supposedly a deep-rooted metaphor for hospitality. \n\nI'm a bit worried that if I change it to something about the sea, it might come across as too superficial or \"touristy.\" I really want to lean into that sense of history and strength. Do you think there's any risk that using the \"desert sun\" phrase would be seen as offensive or dismissive of their identity, or is it actually a safe, high-impact way to show I respect their roots?",
